---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Manifesto — JopChi"
  description="JopChi does not audition for the present. A twice-daily dual-word puzzle that keeps the record without turning that record into a parade."
>
  <article class="manifesto" aria-labelledby="manifesto-heading">
    <p class="section-label">Manifesto</p>
    <h1 id="manifesto-heading">
      <span class="gradient-text">JopChi does not audition for the present.</span>
    </h1>

    <div class="manifesto-body">
      <p>
        It refuses the arms race of polish, the fattening of every tap into a
        campaign, the demand that a pastime shout to be counted. Twice a day the
        rift opens — two hidden words, a narrow window, a single job: find the
        bond between them and close the tear in as few guesses as the mind will
        allow. Then the board goes still. You pick it up. You put it down. It
        keeps the record without turning that record into a parade.
      </p>
      <p>
        Under it runs a score we will not apologize for: the best music ever
        written for two words and a clock. Not a menu loop begging for gold, not
        a trailer wearing an orchestra. A composed weather. It arrives when the
        rift does, and it leaves when you do.
      </p>
      <p>
        The work lives on the pocket screen, patient about sign-in, stubborn
        about the day&rsquo;s two appointments, and built so the puzzle does not
        require one kind of body. Sight is welcome. It is not required. Color is
        a dialect, not a gate. Type grows. Motion can sit down. Contrast can
        shout. Switch and keyboard walk the same board as a thumb. The cosmos of
        two words was never meant to be a private club.
      </p>
    </div>

    <blockquote class="manifesto-pull">
      <p>
        If modern software is a floodlight, JopChi is a lamp you aim yourself.
      </p>
    </blockquote>

    <section aria-labelledby="offers-heading">
      <h2 id="offers-heading">What it offers</h2>
      <ul class="offers-list" role="list">
        <li class="card">
          <strong>Morning Game 1 and Evening Game 2</strong> — two words each,
          one scheduled challenge, no season to enlist in
        </li>
        <li class="card">
          <strong>A ledger of how you showed up</strong>, held back until you
          choose to look
        </li>
        <li class="card">
          <strong>Sound, switch, and stillness</strong> as first-class paths, not
          a retrofit
        </li>
        <li class="card">
          <strong>Palettes, type, and contrast</strong> that follow the player
          instead of scolding them
        </li>
        <li class="card">
          <strong>A soundtrack</strong> that treats a daily puzzle as if it
          deserved a cathedral
        </li>
        <li class="card">
          <strong>No obligation to broadcast</strong>; the session can end in the
          room it began
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <p class="manifesto-footer-note">
      Curious how the accessibility claims are actually implemented? <a href="/accessibility">Read the accessibility page</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .manifesto { max-width: 46rem; }

  .manifesto h1 {
    text-wrap: balance;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  /* Slightly larger, looser measure — this page is meant to be read, not scanned */
  .manifesto-body {
    font-size: 1.1875rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .manifesto-body p {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    /* Avoid single-word last lines in long prose */
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  /* The opening paragraph continues directly from the h1, so it gets a lead-in
     weight rather than a drop cap (which would split the word "It"). */
  .manifesto-body p:first-child {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .manifesto-pull {
    margin: 2.5rem 0;
    padding: 1.75rem 2rem;
    border-left: 4px solid var(--color-accent);
    background: var(--color-bg-surface);
    border-radius: 0 var(--radius-md) var(--radius-md) 0;
  }

  .manifesto-pull p {
    font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 2vw + 0.75rem, 1.625rem);
    line-height: 1.35;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .manifesto section { margin-top: 3rem; }

  .offers-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .offers-list li {
    margin-bottom: 0;
    padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
  }

  .offers-list strong { color: var(--color-accent); }

  .manifesto-footer-note {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .manifesto h1 { margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }

    /* Tighter leading and a smaller lead-in: at this measure the desktop
       values gave an 11-line opening paragraph. The first-child rule has to
       be restated here — it out-specifies .manifesto-body on its own. */
    .manifesto-body { font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.6; }
    .manifesto-body p:first-child { font-size: 1.125rem; }
    .manifesto-body p { margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }

    .manifesto-pull { margin: 2rem 0; padding: 1.25rem 1.25rem; }
    .manifesto section { margin-top: 2.25rem; }
    .offers-list li { padding: 1rem 1.125rem; }
    .manifesto-footer-note { margin-top: 2.25rem; }
  }
</style>
